course: dictionary
lesson: 11484
title: Afflict: trouble that hurts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Afflict is a formal word meaning to cause pain, suffering or trouble. You will meet it in news reports, history books and stories. Look at the clues: «Floods afflict the villages every spring.» Villages do not enjoy floods, so afflict must mean something bad is happening to them.
explain: Afflict is often used in the passive, with «afflicted with» or «afflicted by». «Mia was afflicted with a bad cold for a week.» Being afflicted with a cold means you suffer from it. The clue is the cold: nobody is happy about having one.
explain: Try the swap test. Replace afflict with a simple word like hurt or trouble: «Floods trouble the villages every spring» still makes sense. If your simple word fits, you have found the meaning.
fact: Afflict means to cause pain, suffering or trouble to someone or something.
fact: «Afflicted with» or «afflicted by» means suffering from an illness or problem.
fact: Afflict is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in news, history and stories.
fact: The forms are afflict, afflicts, afflicted and afflicting.
fact: Droughts, floods and diseases are things that can afflict people and places.
exercise: «Floods afflict the villages every spring.» What does afflict mean here? | *To cause trouble or suffering to | To build new houses for | To paint brightly | To wash clean
exercise: «Hundreds of families were afflicted by the drought.» What does afflicted by mean? | Chose, after thinking about the drought | Helped, with food and water | Forgot about the drought | *Suffered from, because of the drought
exercise: «The sailors were afflicted with seasickness.» Find and copy the word that shows they were suffering. | were | sailors | seasickness | *afflicted
test: «The disease afflicted the whole region for years.» What does afflicted mean? | Cured | *Caused suffering to | Made it famous | Hid
test: Which simple word could replace afflict in «Storms afflict the coast»? | Help | *Trouble | Admire | Paint
exam: «Droughts afflict whole regions.» What is the best meaning of afflict here? | Count up | Move away from | *Cause suffering to | Give water to
